{"kind":"doc","text":[
 "P7 stage 1 — the state schema v2 codec (connect/nc_state.h; design docs/plans/2026-10-13-connect-core-p7-state-design.md rev 2).",
 "Hand-specified; read by connect/tests/test_nc_state.c (native, ASan + UBSan) and test/connect-state-wasm.test.js (the wasm, and store.js checkState).",
 "kind project: nc_state_project_json(state, map). expect {status:'ok', nextSeq, header, records:[{id, fp, json}], dropped?, v1?} or {status:'invalid', reason}.",
 "  The result is {status, nextSeq, header, records, dropped} in that order; an expect without dropped means dropped: [] (P7 stage 2, design rev 2.1 item 1: what v2 cannot hold is left out or defaulted and listed, never refused — nc_state.h DROPPED).",
 "  header / json / v1 are the exact canonical TEXTS. With v1: loading the expected records must give {status:'ok', state: v1, map: {fp: id in record order}}, and projecting v1 with that map must give the same result again, with dropped: [] (the canonical form drops nothing).",
 "kind load: nc_state_load_json({header, records:[{id, json}]}). expect {status:'ok', state, map} or {status:'damaged', reason}.",
 "TOKENS, expanded by both runners in every string of a vector (texts, ids, fps, map keys and values) before use:",
 "  #1# = '1' x 128 (the own ID), #A# #B# #C# #D# #E# = 'a'..'e' x 128, #V# = '9' x 128, #W# = '8' x 128 (vault addresses),",
 "  #SA# #SB# #SC# = 'a' 'b' 'c' x 64 (salts), #G# = 'f' x 64 (a group id),",
 "  #<p><n># with <p> one of c p v g = <p> followed by <n> zero-padded to 20 digits (#c7# = c00000000000000000007).",
 "fills: {'<token>': [[fp, count], ...]} — the JSON string '<token>' (quotes included) stands for a JSON array of those fps, each repeated count times, in order. Fills are expanded before tokens.",
 "The node runner also checks every project vector against the REAL store.js checkState: it must throw exactly when reason is 'checkState' (reason 'json' is not checked: JSON.parse itself refuses)."
]},

